diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..bca87cf 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,39 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Use Node.js 24 or later. Run `pnpm install`, `pnpm build`, then `pnpm start`.
+The app is served at `http://localhost:11224/devtools-times/`.
+
+Registration supports either a discoverable passkey or a password. Sign-in supports
+passkeys without entering a username, as well as password fallback. Account security
+at `/devtools-times/account/security` lets signed-in users add, rename, and remove
+passkeys, see their creation and last-use dates, and reauthenticate. Sensitive changes
+require verification within the last five minutes. A passwordless account cannot
+remove its last passkey. There is no account recovery flow; add a second passkey or
+use a synced password manager to avoid losing access.
+
+The old remote demo login/register calls have been replaced with local server-side
+accounts. Remote demo accounts are not migrated; register a new account locally.
+Passwords use salted scrypt hashes. Session tokens are stored as hashes, with
+HttpOnly, SameSite cookies (Secure over HTTPS). WebAuthn uses SimpleWebAuthn for
+signature, origin, RP ID, and required user-verification checks. Challenges expire
+after five minutes and are consumed once, including on failed verification.
+
+Deployment settings:
+
+- `AUTH_ORIGIN`: the public origin, e.g. `https://news.example.com` (no path). Set
+  explicitly in production, especially behind a reverse proxy. Defaults to the
+  request origin. Passkeys require HTTPS except on localhost.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: SQLite file path, defaults to `./data/auth.sqlite`. Mount a
+  persistent writable volume and back it up. This implementation supports a single
+  application instance; multiple replicas need a shared database implementation.
+- Keep the same public hostname: passkeys are bound to its RP ID.
+
+Run `pnpm test` to build and execute API integration tests using generated ES256
+keys and real signed WebAuthn attestation/assertion data. Tests cover registration,
+authentication, replay and forgery rejection, management, reauthentication, ownership,
+password fallback, logout, and protection against removing the last sign-in method.
+No manual browser verification is required.
